<title>UK: Goldman Sachs set &quot;COOL' warrants on 2026 T-Bond.</title>
<headline>Goldman Sachs set &quot;COOL' warrants on 2026 T-Bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Godman Sachs (London) said it has issued 20 million European-style call and put warrants, in four equal tranches, on the U.S. Treasury bond due August 2026.</p>
<p>Each warrant controls $100 principle amount of the U.S.</p>
<p>Treasury bond</p>
<p>* * * * * * *</p>
<p>   TYPE	   EXPIRY    STRIKE     REBATE LEVEL</p>
<p>   CALL	  14.AUG.97  103.O PCT  98.00 PCT</p>
<p>   CALL	  14.AUG.97  105.0 PCT  100.0 PCT</p>
<p>   PUT	   14.AUG.97  100.0 PCT  108.00 PCT</p>
<p>   PUT	   14.AUG.97  99.00 PCT  106.0 PCT</p>
<p>* * * * * * *</p>
<p>NOTES    EACH WARRANT ENTITLES THE HOLDER TO RECEIVE POSITIVE</p>
<p>(CALLS) OR NEGATIVE (PUTS) THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN THE U.S</p>
<p>TREASURY BONDS AND THE STRIKE ON THE MATURITY DATE. FURTHERMORE</p>
<p>THE HOLDER WILL BE PAID $10.0 PER WARRANT, IF THE U.S. TREASURY</p>
<p>BOND PRICE IS NEVER BELOW (CALL) OR ABOVE (PUT) THE REBATE LEVEL</p>
<p>AT ANY TIME FROM THE LAUNCH DATE TO THE EXPIRY DATE.</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
